  "reason": "Evidence: The top-3 performers (config_012: 0.7250, config_029: 0.7207, config_019: 0.7131) all use scvi_n200 + transformer aggregation, with imagenet_vit_l outperforming resnet50. Weighted fusion slightly edges concat. The best configuration (config_012) is already identified. Question: config_042 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + concat) is the only untested cell in the 2×2 aggregation×fusion matrix for the best RNA+image encoder pair. While avgpool is expected to underperform transformer (~2% gap seen in config_001 vs config_012), testing this completes the design space for the top component combination and confirms whether the transformer advantage is consistent across fusion strategies. Rationale: As the final experiment (10/10), this provides the most informative closure on the primary design question (aggregation × fusion interaction for the best encoders) without wasting a slot on a configuration with weak prior evidence (scgpt or pca_n2000 RNA encoders, singleprofile, or unimodal settings all showed substantially lower performance)."
}

